# Key fixups for the remote control, matched on the receiver's USB ids.
#
# HAOBO 4842:0001 is the dongle for the G20-style air-mouse remote. Its OK
# button reports HID consumer usage 0x0c/0x41 ("Menu Pick"), which the kernel
# translates to KEY_SELECT. xkb's evdev keycode table has an entry for that
# code but no symbols file binds a keysym to it, so every Wayland client gets a
# keypress it cannot name: Chromium never raises an "Enter" DOM event and the
# tile under the cursor never opens. The button looks dead, and in mouse mode
# it appears to recover only because the remote sends a left click instead.
#
# Nothing downstream can repair this. By the time labwc or the page sees the
# event the key is already nameless, so the remap has to happen here, while
# evdev still has the raw scancode in hand.
#
# The remote's other buttons emit codes that do have keysyms, so they are bound
# in labwc or handled in index.html rather than rewritten here.
#
# The mic button is remapped to Back for a different reason. Turning the
# remote's mouse mode on repurposes the D-pad as a pointer, OK as a left click
# and the back arrow as a right click, so in that mode the remote has no back
# key at all. Netflix's main page is close to unusable without a pointer: its
# tiles expand when the selection rests on one and then trap it, so mouse mode
# is the practical way to browse, and that is exactly where back went missing.
# The mic button keeps sending a key in both modes and had nothing bound to it,
# so it becomes the back button that works while browsing.
#
# The version field is deliberately left out of the match so a firmware
# revision on the dongle does not silently drop the rule.
evdev:input:b0003v4842p0001*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_c0041=enter
 KEYBOARD_KEY_c00cf=back
